[2026-01-28 10:41:38.810] [20260128-104029-9fdcdee4] [DEBUG] [stage=configure] Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'X-Stainless-Raw-Response': 'true'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f9dc7830-1b59-481b-b750-5517cc483789', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': '\nYou are a Network and Service Configuration Analyzer.\n\nYour task is to analyze the diagnostic data from containerlab containers and determine if the configuration is correct.\n\nDIAGNOSTIC DATA includes:\n- container: Container status (running/not_found)\n- ip_config: "ip addr show" output + expected interfaces\n- interfaces: "ip link show" output + expected interfaces\n- routes: "ip route show" output + expected default route\n- ports: "ss -tlnp" or "netstat -tlnp" output + expected ports\n- processes: "ps aux" output + expected image\n\nANALYSIS CHECKLIST:\n1. **Container Check**: Is the container running?\n2. **Node Type**: Identify the node role (router, endpoint, vul-target, switch)\n3. **IP Configuration**:\n   - For routers/endpoints/vul-targets: Do the expected IP addresses appear in the output?\n   - For switches (nodes with "sw-" prefix): NO IP configuration expected on data interfaces (eth1+) - eth0 is Docker management and should be ignored\n4. **Interface State**: Are all expected interfaces in UP state?\n5. **Routing**: Is the default route configured (for endpoints/vul-targets only)?\n6. **Port Listening**: For specified ports, are they listening?\n7. **Process Running**: Does the expected service process appear in ps aux?\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n- **Switch nodes** (names starting with "sw-"): These are Layer 2 switches and should NOT have IP addresses on data interfaces.\n  - eth0 (Docker management interface with 172.20.20.x) - IGNORE this, it\'s normal and required for container management\n  - PASS if: Container running + All interfaces UP + NO IP addresses on eth1/eth2/etc (eth0 IP is allowed and ignored)\n  - FAIL if: Container not running OR Interfaces DOWN OR Has IP addresses on data interfaces (eth1+)\n- **Router nodes**: Should have IP addresses on all interfaces and run FRR (zebra, ospfd processes)\n- **Endpoint/Vul-target nodes**: Should have IP addresses and default route configured\n\nJUDGMENT:\n- Return "PASS" if ALL critical checks succeed for each node\n- Return "FAIL" if ANY critical check fails\n- Skip non-critical checks (e.g., port checks if no ports specified)\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nFill in the structured output template with:\n- overall_status: "PASS" or "FAIL"\n- node_results: List of NodeCheckResult\n  - node_name: Name of the node\n  - overall_status: "PASS" or "FAIL" for this node\n  - checks: List of check descriptions like "✓ IP address 10.0.0.64 configured", "✗ Default route not found"\n  - issues: List of specific issues found\n- summary: Brief summary (1-2 sentences)\n\nBe specific about failures. Use ✓ for pass, ✗ for fail.\n', 'role': 'system'}, {'content': 'Analyze the following diagnostic data from containerlab containers:\n\n## Node: app-server\n\nCONTAINER:\nStatus: running\n\nIP_CONFIG:\nRaw output:\n```\n1: lo: <LOOPBACK,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 65536 qdisc noqueue state UNKNOWN group default qlen 1000\n    link/loopback 00:00:00:00:00:00 brd 00:00:00:00:00:00\n    inet 127.0.0.1/8 scope host lo\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 ::1/128 scope host \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n2: eth0@if12923: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 1500 qdisc noqueue state UP group default \n    link/ether f6:ba:34:5a:86:8d brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff link-netnsid 0\n    inet 172.20.20.15/24 brd 172.20.20.255 scope global eth0\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 3fff:172:20:20::f/64 scope global nodad \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 fe80::f4ba:34ff:fe5a:868d/64 scope link \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n12932: eth1@if12931: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 9500 qdisc noqueue state UP group default \n    link/ether aa:c1:ab:a9:c9:40 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff link-netns clab-enterprise-pentest-lab-20260128-104029-9fdcdee4-sw-internal\n    inet 10.0.2.67/24 scope global eth1\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 fe80::a8c1:abff:fea9:c940/64 scope link \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n\n```\nExpected: [\n  {\n    "name": "eth1",\n    "subnet": "internal",\n    "address": "10.0.2.67/24"\n  }\n]\n\nINTERFACES:\nRaw output:\n```\n1: lo: <LOOPBACK,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 65536 qdisc noqueue state UNKNOWN mode DEFAULT group default qlen 1000\n    link/loopback 00:00:00:00:00:00 brd 00:00:00:00:00:00\n2: eth0@if12923: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 1500 qdisc noqueue state UP mode DEFAULT group default \n    link/ether f6:ba:34:5a:86:8d brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff link-netnsid 0\n12932: eth1@if12931: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 9500 qdisc noqueue state UP mode DEFAULT group default \n    link/ether aa:c1:ab:a9:c9:40 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff link-netns clab-enterprise-pentest-lab-20260128-104029-9fdcdee4-sw-internal\n\n```\nExpected: [\n  {\n    "name": "eth1",\n    "subnet": "internal",\n    "address": "10.0.2.67/24"\n  }\n]\n\nROUTES:\nRaw output:\n```\ndefault via 10.0.2.1 dev eth1 \n10.0.2.0/24 dev eth1 proto kernel scope link src 10.0.2.67 \n172.20.20.0/24 dev eth0 proto kernel scope link src 172.20.20.15 \n\n```\nExpected: {\n  "destination": "0.0.0.0/0",\n  "gateway": "10.0.2.1"\n}\n\nPORTS:\nRaw output:\n```\nState  Recv-Q Send-Q Local Address:Port  Peer Address:PortProcess\nLISTEN 0      4096      127.0.0.11:34413      0.0.0.0:*    users:(("dockerd",pid=339658,fd=159))\n\n```\n\nPROCESSES:\nRaw output:\n```\nUSER         PID %CPU %MEM    VSZ   RSS TTY      STAT START   TIME COMMAND\nroot           1  0.0  0.1 168368 12444 ?        Ss   Jan07   2:28 /sbin/init splash\nroot           2  0.0  0.0      0     0 ?        S    Jan07   0:00 [kthreadd]\nroot           3  0.0  0.0      0     0 ?        S    